# Portfolio performance guardrails

When adding or editing motion, video, canvas, or heavy media, follow `.cursor/skills/portfolio-performance/SKILL.md` and `specs/11-performance-budget.md`.

## Must

- One primary motion system per viewport; pause/hide offscreen work (IntersectionObserver)
- One global canvas; particle caps (desktop ≤3k, mobile ≤1k or off); ambient 24–30fps
- Max 1–2 videos decoding; poster + `preload="none"`; play visible/hover only
- Scroll animation: `transform` + `opacity` only
- Lazy load below-fold media; dynamic import for interaction-only heavy components
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — remove ambient animation

## Do not

- Stack multiple full-viewport animated canvases or ambient loops
- Run rAF loops when element is offscreen
- Animate `filter: blur()`, width/height/top/left, or box-shadow on scroll
- Autoplay video without poster or offscreen pause
- Load all font weights or uncompressed video larger than display size

## Visual alignment

Performance constraints pair with `.cursor/skills/portfolio-visual/SKILL.md` — reduce scope, do not break the warm editorial feel with extra motion layers.
